iris: always prefer 4K tiles for memory objects

Chrome draws WebGPU with Dawn on anv and composites it with Skia on
iris, and hands each frame across as a memory object, an opaque file
descriptor with no DRM modifier. Both drivers must then pick the same
tiling from the same flags. anv asks ISL to prefer 4K alignment for
such an image, so it gets Tile4. iris meant to do the same, but on
Xe2+ a memory object is always PIPE_BIND_SHARED, so the branch before
it, which only turns compression off, matched first and the else-if
that adds the preference never ran. ISL then took Tile64 wherever it
cost under 10% more memory, and iris read Tile64 from memory anv wrote
as Tile4: a checkerboard over WebGPU canvases of most sizes.
The preference now stands apart from that chain. Mesa's main has the
same code; 9826b6081da added the preference.

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/iris/iris_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/iris/iris_resource.c
index 35ed914..ac1d33d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/iris/iris_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/iris/iris_resource.c
@@ -915,14 +915,20 @@ iris_resource_configure_main(const struct iris_screen *screen,
             (templ->bind & PIPE_BIND_SHARED))
       usage |= ISL_SURF_USAGE_DISABLE_AUX_BIT;
 
-   else if (!res->mod_info && res->external_format != PIPE_FORMAT_NONE) {
+   else if (templ->bind & PIPE_BIND_CONST_BW)
+      usage |= ISL_SURF_USAGE_DISABLE_AUX_BIT;
+
+   /* A memory object carries no modifier, so its tiling must be the one anv
+    * picks for the same image, which prefers 4K tiles. On Xe2+ a memory
+    * object is always PIPE_BIND_SHARED, so this can't be an else of the
+    * branch above: there it never ran, and iris read a Tile64 layout from
+    * memory anv wrote as Tile4.
+    */
+   if (!res->mod_info && res->external_format != PIPE_FORMAT_NONE) {
       usage |= ISL_SURF_USAGE_DISABLE_AUX_BIT;
       usage |= ISL_SURF_USAGE_PREFER_4K_ALIGNMENT;
    }
 
-   else if (templ->bind & PIPE_BIND_CONST_BW)
-      usage |= ISL_SURF_USAGE_DISABLE_AUX_BIT;
-
    if (templ->usage == PIPE_USAGE_STAGING)
       usage |= ISL_SURF_USAGE_STAGING_BIT;
 
